Sval: mach keeps its last five build and test profiles

mach keeps a resource profile of every build and test run in its state
directory's logs/build and logs/test, and a warnings file of every build.
It trims its per-command logs with _cleanup_old_logs, but nothing trims
these, and a test run's profile reaches tens of megabytes. An objdir kept
across builds, as on a CI runner whose tree persists, fills its disk with
them. Both writers call the same cleanup, which keeps the five newest of
each kind.

